# Steamworks: Steam app id

Use one app id everywhere: steam_appid.txt, the SDK init call, engine settings and SteamPipe scripts must match the app in Steamworks. 480 (Spacewar) is Valve's test app and never belongs in a release build.

## The test app id 480 (Spacewar) is still set (warning)

- Why: 480 is Valve's public test app. A build that starts with it shows up as Spacewar, and its achievements and stats go to Spacewar instead of your game.
- Fix: Replace 480 with your game's app id (apps.main.appid in steamworks.yaml) before uploading a build.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary

## An app id differs from the game's app ids (error)

- Why: The SDK, the build scripts and Steamworks must agree on the app id, or the game starts as another app and builds land in the wrong place.
- Fix: Use the app id of the main game, its demo or its playtest (apps.*.appid in steamworks.yaml) everywhere.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/sdk/api#SteamAPI_RestartAppIfNecessary

With the steamworks-mcp server connected, `check_code(path)` finds these problems in the whole project, with file and line (`check_code(path, rules=["steamworks-app-id"])` for this group only).
